  "content": {
    "id": "p39-q12-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "12",
    "prompt": "State the natural domain of these functions.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p39-q12-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=\\dfrac{\\sqrt{x}}{x-2}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$[0,2)\\cup(2,\\infty)$",
          "worked": "The radicand must be non-negative and the denominator non-zero.\n$$\\begin{align*}x&\\ge 0\\\\x-2&\\ne 0\\\\x&\\ne 2\\end{align*}$$\nDomain: $[0,2)\\cup(2,\\infty)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      },
      {
        "id": "p39-q12-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=\\dfrac{\\sqrt{x+1}}{x-2}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$[-1,2)\\cup(2,\\infty)$",
          "worked": "The radicand must be non-negative and the denominator non-zero.\n$$\\begin{align*}x+1&\\ge 0\\\\x&\\ge -1\\\\x-2&\\ne 0\\\\x&\\ne 2\\end{align*}$$\nDomain: $[-1,2)\\cup(2,\\infty)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      },
      {
        "id": "p39-q12-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=\\sqrt{x+1}+\\sqrt{5-x}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$[-1,5]$",
          "worked": "Both radicands must be non-negative.\n$$\\begin{align*}x+1&\\ge 0\\\\x&\\ge -1\\\\5-x&\\ge 0\\\\x&\\le 5\\end{align*}$$\nDomain: $[-1,5]$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      },
      {
        "id": "p39-q12-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=\\sqrt{x+1}+\\sqrt{3-x}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$[-1,3]$",
          "worked": "Both radicands must be non-negative.\n$$\\begin{align*}x+1&\\ge 0\\\\x&\\ge -1\\\\3-x&\\ge 0\\\\x&\\le 3\\end{align*}$$\nDomain: $[-1,3]$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      },
      {
        "id": "p39-q12-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{x+1}}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x>-1$",
          "worked": "The square root is in the denominator, so its radicand must be positive.\n$$\\begin{align*}x+1&>0\\\\x&>-1\\end{align*}$$\nDomain: $(-1,\\infty)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p39-q12-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{3-x}}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x<3$",
          "worked": "The square root is in the denominator, so its radicand must be positive.\n$$\\begin{align*}3-x&>0\\\\x&<3\\end{align*}$$\nDomain: $(-\\infty,3)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p39-q12-g",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "g",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=\\sqrt{x+1}+\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{5-x}}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$[-1,5)$",
          "worked": "The first radicand must be non-negative; the radicand in the denominator must be positive.\n$$\\begin{align*}x+1&\\ge 0\\\\x&\\ge -1\\\\5-x&>0\\\\x&<5\\end{align*}$$\nDomain: $[-1,5)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      },
      {
        "id": "p39-q12-h",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "h",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=\\sqrt{x+4}+\\dfrac{1}{x-1}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$[-4,1)\\cup(1,\\infty)$",
          "worked": "The radicand must be non-negative and the denominator non-zero.\n$$\\begin{align*}x+4&\\ge 0\\\\x&\\ge -4\\\\x-1&\\ne 0\\\\x&\\ne 1\\end{align*}$$\nDomain: $[-4,1)\\cup(1,\\infty)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      },
      {
        "id": "p39-q12-i",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "i",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=\\dfrac{\\sqrt{x+3}}{x-1}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$[-3,1)\\cup(1,\\infty)$",
          "worked": "The radicand must be non-negative and the denominator non-zero.\n$$\\begin{align*}x+3&\\ge 0\\\\x&\\ge -3\\\\x-1&\\ne 0\\\\x&\\ne 1\\end{align*}$$\nDomain: $[-3,1)\\cup(1,\\infty)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      },
      {
        "id": "p39-q12-j",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "j",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=\\dfrac{\\sqrt{x+3}}{x+1}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$[-3,-1)\\cup(-1,\\infty)$",
          "worked": "The radicand must be non-negative and the denominator non-zero.\n$$\\begin{align*}x+3&\\ge 0\\\\x&\\ge -3\\\\x+1&\\ne 0\\\\x&\\ne -1\\end{align*}$$\nDomain: $[-3,-1)\\cup(-1,\\infty)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      },
      {
        "id": "p39-q12-k",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "k",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=\\dfrac{\\sqrt{5-x}}{x+1}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(-\\infty,-1)\\cup(-1,5]$",
          "worked": "The radicand must be non-negative and the denominator non-zero.\n$$\\begin{align*}5-x&\\ge 0\\\\x&\\le 5\\\\x+1&\\ne 0\\\\x&\\ne -1\\end{align*}$$\nDomain: $(-\\infty,-1)\\cup(-1,5]$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      },
      {
        "id": "p39-q12-l",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "l",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=\\dfrac{\\sqrt{5-x}}{x-6}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(-\\infty,5]$",
          "worked": "The radicand must be non-negative and the denominator non-zero.\n$$\\begin{align*}5-x&\\ge 0\\\\x&\\le 5\\\\x-6&\\ne 0\\\\x&\\ne 6\\end{align*}$$\nThe condition $x\\le 5$ already excludes $6$.\nDomain: $(-\\infty,5]$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      }
    ]
  },
